Anthropic claude-code-security-review (MIT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

skills/review-security/prompts/reviewer.md and
skills/review-security/prompts/false-positives.md are derived from
.claude/commands/security-review.md in
https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code-security-review (commit c19afa7).
The candidate -> parallel per-finding verification -> confidence >= 8
pipeline follows that command's three-step analysis.

Modifications from the original:
  - Split into a reviewer prompt and a shared false-positive prompt so the
    same exclusions and precedents reach the reviewer and every verifier.
  - Replaced Claude Code `!`command`` context injection and sub-task steps
    with instructions for standalone read-only agents run by a script.
  - Added SSRF, IDOR, and mass-assignment categories, a prompt-injection
    rule, a required parseable heading format, and Source/Sink/Confidence
    fields per finding.
  - Added a pre-existing-issue exclusion, and carved dependency-audit hits
    for dependencies this diff adds out of the outdated-library exclusion.
  - Fixed typos and duplicated list numbering.

